IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Act 1947 (Singapore) -- what an individual must do and what can be done to them: telling the Comptroller I am
-- chargeable (s 62(4), (5)), objecting to my assessment (s 76(2)-(4)), appealing to the Board of Review (s 79), paying
-- (s 85) and what is added if I pay late (s 87), being stopped from leaving Singapore (s 86), and what I can be made to pay
-- for an offence (ss 94, 94A, 95, 96, 96A, 98).
--
-- SEAT: the individual taxpayer -- a person, resident or not, assessed or assessable to income tax for one year of assessment.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, version in force from 11/9/2026, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ITA1947.txt.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the Comptroller's notices and powers to call for returns and information (ss 62(1)-(3), 63-65K) beyond
-- their effect on me; the form of returns; partnerships (s 71); additional assessments and their time limits (s 74);
-- hearing of appeals and appeals to the High Court (ss 80-84); deduction from emoluments (s 91); repayment (s 93); the PIC
-- bonus limbs of ss 95-96A (the scheme is tied to years of assessment before 2024); offences by officers (s 97); rules
-- under s 76(9) substituting a longer objection period (not in the deposit -- an input here).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual taxpayer, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Act 1947 -- my duties, deadlines and penalties`

§§ `s 62(4), (5) -- telling the Comptroller I am chargeable`

-- s 62(4): "Every person chargeable with tax for any year of assessment who has not been required within 3 months after the
-- commencement of such year of assessment to make a return of the person's income for that year as provided in subsection (1)
-- or (3) must, within 14 days after the end of that period, give notice to the Comptroller that the person is so chargeable."
-- (5): "Any individual who arrives in Singapore during any year of assessment must give such notice within one month of the
-- date of the individual's arrival."
-- Gloss: if I owe tax and have not been asked for a return by the end of March, I must say so myself within 14 days; a new
-- arrival has one month from arriving.
-- Inference: the 3-month period from 1 January ends on 31 March, so "14 days after the end of that period" is 14 April.
-- Inference: where (5) applies, its one month replaces the 14 days of (4).
DECLARE `Notice deadline` IS ONE OF
    `no notice is needed`
    `by 14 April of the year of assessment`
    `within one month of my arrival in Singapore`

GIVEN `I am chargeable with tax for the year of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was required to make a return within the first 3 months of the year of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I arrived in Singapore during the year of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Notice deadline`
DECIDE `By when must I tell the Comptroller I am chargeable` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `I am chargeable with tax for the year of assessment` THEN `no notice is needed`
        IF `I was required to make a return within the first 3 months of the year of assessment` THEN `no notice is needed`
        IF `I arrived in Singapore during the year of assessment` THEN `within one month of my arrival in Singapore`
        OTHERWISE `by 14 April of the year of assessment`

§§ `s 76(2)-(4) -- objecting to my assessment`

-- s 76(2): "If any person disputes the assessment, the person may apply to the Comptroller, by written notice of objection, to
-- review and to revise the assessment". (3): the application "must state precisely the grounds" and be made within "(a) if the
-- person is a company ..., 2 months; or (b) in any other case, 30 days, from the date of the service of the notice of
-- assessment." (4): "The Comptroller upon being satisfied that, owing to absence, sickness or other reasonable cause, the
-- person disputing the assessment was prevented from making the application within the period ..., must extend the period
-- as may be reasonable in the circumstances." (9): the Minister may by rules "substitute a longer period".
-- Gloss: I have 30 days from service to object in writing with precise grounds; if absence, sickness or another reasonable
-- cause stopped me, the Comptroller must give me more time once satisfied of it.
-- The Comptroller's satisfaction is an input. A period substituted by rules under s 76(9) is a MAYBE input (none is in the
-- deposit).
GIVEN `days since the notice of assessment was served on me` IS A NUMBER
      `a longer period substituted by rules under s 76(9)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `my objection states precisely my grounds` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Comptroller is satisfied absence, sickness or other reasonable cause prevented me, and I am within the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my objection in time and in form` IF
        `my objection states precisely my grounds`
    AND (    `days since the notice of assessment was served on me` AT MOST `the objection period`
         OR  `the Comptroller is satisfied absence, sickness or other reasonable cause prevented me, and I am within the extension`)
    WHERE
        `the objection period` MEANS
            CONSIDER `a longer period substituted by rules under s 76(9)`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 30
            WHEN JUST days THEN days

§§ `s 79 -- appealing to the Board of Review`

-- s 79(1): a person aggrieved who "has failed to agree with the Comptroller in the manner provided in section 76(6) may appeal to
-- the Board by lodging with the secretary -- (a) within 30 days after the date of the Comptroller's refusal to amend the
-- assessment, a notice of appeal; and (b) within 30 days after the date on which the notice of appeal was lodged, a petition of
-- appeal containing a statement of the grounds of appeal." (3): "The notice of appeal is deemed to be withdrawn if no petition of
-- appeal ... is lodged". (11): the Chairperson "may, in his or her discretion" permit a late appeal "if it is shown to the
-- Chairperson's satisfaction that the person was prevented ... owing to absence, sickness or other reasonable cause and that
-- there has been no unreasonable delay".
-- Gloss: two 30-day steps -- a notice of appeal after the refusal, then a petition after the notice; miss the second and the
-- notice is treated as withdrawn. Lateness can be forgiven, but only at the Chairperson's discretion.
-- The Chairperson's permission is an input. A petition not lodged at all is NOTHING in its days.
GIVEN `days from the Comptroller's refusal to amend to my notice of appeal` IS A NUMBER
      `days from my notice of appeal to my petition of appeal` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the Chairperson has permitted me to proceed out of time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my appeal to the Board go ahead` IF
        `the Chairperson has permitted me to proceed out of time`
    OR  (    `days from the Comptroller's refusal to amend to my notice of appeal` AT MOST 30
         AND `the petition was lodged in time`)
    WHERE
        `the petition was lodged in time` MEANS
            CONSIDER `days from my notice of appeal to my petition of appeal`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST days THEN days AT MOST 30

-- The same two steps as a regulative rule, from my seat: a permission to lodge a notice within 30 days, which, once used,
-- becomes a duty to lodge the petition within 30 days of it. Not using the permission leaves the assessment standing; missing
-- the petition is the deemed withdrawal of s 79(3).
DECLARE `Party to an appeal` IS ONE OF `the aggrieved taxpayer`
DECLARE `Step in an appeal` IS ONE OF `lodge a notice of appeal`, `lodge a petition of appeal`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party to an appeal` `Step in an appeal`
DECIDE `my appeal to the Board of Review` IS
    PARTY  `the aggrieved taxpayer`
    MAY    `lodge a notice of appeal`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE  PARTY  `the aggrieved taxpayer`
           MUST   `lodge a petition of appeal`
           WITHIN 30
           HENCE  FULFILLED
           LEST   BREACH BY `the aggrieved taxpayer`

§§ `s 85 -- when I must pay`

-- s 85(1): tax "is, despite any objection or appeal against the assessment on which the tax is levied, payable at the place
-- stated in the notice given under section 76 within one month after the service of the notice." (2): the Comptroller "may, in
-- his or her discretion and subject to such terms and conditions, including the imposition of interest, ... extend the time".
-- Gloss: an objection or appeal does not put off payment: I pay within a month of the notice unless the Comptroller extends.
GIVEN `I have objected or appealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my objection or appeal put off when I must pay` IF FALSE

GIVEN `I paid within one month after service of the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Comptroller extended my time and I paid within the extension` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Did I pay in time` IF
        `I paid within one month after service of the notice`
    OR  `the Comptroller extended my time and I paid within the extension`

§§ `s 86 -- being stopped from leaving Singapore`

-- s 86(1): "Where the Comptroller is of the opinion that any person is about or likely to leave Singapore without paying all tax
-- assessed upon the person, the Comptroller may issue a certificate ... and a direction ... that such person be prevented from
-- leaving Singapore without paying the tax or furnishing security to the Comptroller's satisfaction". (4): payment, or a
-- certificate that the tax "has been paid or secured", is sufficient authority to let the person leave.
-- Gloss: if I have unpaid tax and the Comptroller thinks I may leave without paying, I can be stopped at the border until I pay
-- or give security. The Comptroller's opinion and the security's acceptability are inputs.
GIVEN `I have tax assessed that is unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Comptroller is of the opinion I am about or likely to leave without paying` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have paid or furnished security to the Comptroller's satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be prevented from leaving Singapore` IF
        `I have tax assessed that is unpaid`
    AND `the Comptroller is of the opinion I am about or likely to leave without paying`
    AND NOT `I have paid or furnished security to the Comptroller's satisfaction`

§§ `s 87 -- what is added if I pay late`

-- s 87(1): "if any tax is not paid within the periods prescribed in section 85 -- (a) a sum equal to 5% of the amount of tax
-- payable is added thereto; ... (c) ... if the amount of tax outstanding is not paid within 60 days of the imposition of the
-- penalty as provided by paragraph (a), an additional penalty of 1% of the tax outstanding is payable for each completed month
-- that the tax remains unpaid, but the total additional penalty must not exceed 12% of the amount of tax outstanding".
-- (2): "The Comptroller may for any good cause shown remit the whole or any part of the penalty".
-- Gloss: 5% at once if I am late; if still unpaid 60 days after that, 1% more for each full month, capped at 12%. The
-- Comptroller may let me off, so these are the most that can be added.
-- Inference: the completed months are counted as an input, since the text does not say whether they run from the end of the
-- 60 days or from the 5% penalty.
GIVEN `my tax payable` IS A NUMBER
      `I paid in time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I paid within 60 days of the 5% penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tax outstanding` IS A NUMBER
      `completed months the tax has remained unpaid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most that can be added to my tax for paying late` IS
    IF `I paid in time` THEN 0
    ELSE `my tax payable` TIMES 5% PLUS `the additional penalty`
    WHERE
        `the additional penalty` MEANS
            IF `I paid within 60 days of the 5% penalty` THEN 0
            ELSE `the tax outstanding` TIMES `the additional rate`
        `the additional rate` MEANS
            IF `completed months the tax has remained unpaid` TIMES 1% AT MOST 12%
            THEN `completed months the tax has remained unpaid` TIMES 1%
            ELSE 12%

§§ `ss 94, 94A, 95, 96, 96A, 98 -- what I can be made to pay for an offence`

-- s 94(2): an offence "for which no other penalty is provided" -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 and in default of payment to
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months".
-- s 94A(1): failing "without reasonable excuse to comply with any provision of section 62" -- a fine not exceeding $5,000, in
-- default 6 months. (3): failing for "2 years or more" -- "a penalty equal to double the amount of tax which the Comptroller
-- assesses ... and a fine not exceeding $5,000".
-- s 95(1): an incorrect return or information -- "a penalty equal to the amount of tax ... undercharged". (2): the same
-- "without reasonable excuse or through negligence" -- "a penalty equal to double" the tax undercharged, "and shall also be
-- liable to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both".
-- s 96(1): wilfully with intent to evade, omitting income, making a false statement or giving a false answer -- "a penalty of
-- treble" the tax undercharged, and "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years or ...
-- both".
-- s 96A(1): wilfully with intent to evade, keeping false books or using "any fraud, art or contrivance" -- "a penalty of 4
-- times" the tax undercharged, and "a fine not exceeding $50,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or ...
-- both".
-- s 98(1): obstructing the Comptroller or an officer -- "a fine not exceeding $10,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not
-- exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- Gloss: the multiple of the tax undercharged rises with culpability: once for an incorrect return, twice for negligence,
-- three times for wilful evasion, four times for fraud. Most of these offences may be compounded by the Comptroller (ss 94(6),
-- 94A(5), 95(3), 96(4), 96A(4), 98(2)); the figures are what I can be made to pay on conviction.
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `a contravention with no other penalty provided`
    `failing without reasonable excuse to give notice or make a return`
    `failing without reasonable excuse to make a return for 2 years or more`
    `an incorrect return`
    `an incorrect return without reasonable excuse or through negligence`
    `wilfully omitting income or making a false statement with intent to evade tax`
    `wilfully keeping false books or using fraud with intent to evade tax`
    `obstructing the Comptroller or an officer`

DECLARE Exposure HAS
    `times the tax`                            IS A NUMBER
    `fine up to`                               IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment up to, in months`            IS A NUMBER
    `imprisonment only in default of payment`  IS A BOOLEAN

-- The penalty multiple of s 94A(3) is of the tax the Comptroller assesses "to the best of the Comptroller's judgment"; that
-- tax is the input for it.
GIVEN `what I did` IS A Conduct
GIVETH AN Exposure
DECIDE `What is my exposure for` `what I did` IS
    CONSIDER `what I did`
    --                                                                                          times tax, fine,  months, default only
    WHEN `a contravention with no other penalty provided`                            THEN Exposure OF 0, 5_000,  6,  TRUE
    WHEN `failing without reasonable excuse to give notice or make a return`         THEN Exposure OF 0, 5_000,  6,  TRUE
    WHEN `failing without reasonable excuse to make a return for 2 years or more`    THEN Exposure OF 2, 5_000,  6,  TRUE
    WHEN `an incorrect return`                                                       THEN Exposure OF 1, 0,      0,  FALSE
    WHEN `an incorrect return without reasonable excuse or through negligence`       THEN Exposure OF 2, 5_000,  36, FALSE
    WHEN `wilfully omitting income or making a false statement with intent to evade tax` THEN Exposure OF 3, 10_000, 36, FALSE
    WHEN `wilfully keeping false books or using fraud with intent to evade tax`      THEN Exposure OF 4, 50_000, 60, FALSE
    WHEN `obstructing the Comptroller or an officer`                                 THEN Exposure OF 0, 10_000, 12, FALSE

GIVEN `what I did` IS A Conduct
      `the tax undercharged` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What penalty must I pay on conviction for` `what I did` `the tax undercharged` IS
    (`What is my exposure for` `what I did`)'s `times the tax` TIMES `the tax undercharged`

GIVEN `what I did` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for` `what I did` IS
    (`What is my exposure for` `what I did`)'s `fine up to`

GIVEN `what I did` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for, in months` `what I did` IS
    (`What is my exposure for` `what I did`)'s `imprisonment up to, in months`

-- s 94A(2): after a second or subsequent conviction for failing to comply with s 62 "in respect of the same year of
-- assessment, the person shall be liable to a further penalty of $100 for every day during which the offence is continued
-- after such conviction."
-- Gloss: keep failing after a repeat conviction for the same year and it costs up to $100 a day more.
-- Only limb (b) (second or subsequent conviction under s 62 or 71(1)) is encoded.
GIVEN `my convictions under s 94A for the same year of assessment` IS A NUMBER
      `days I have continued the failure since the latest conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What further daily penalty can I be made to pay` IS
    IF `my convictions under s 94A for the same year of assessment` AT LEAST 2
    THEN 100 TIMES `days I have continued the failure since the latest conviction`
    ELSE 0

-- s 96(2): when an individual has been convicted for "(a) 3 or more offences under this section ...; or (b) one offence under
-- this section and one offence under section 96A", imprisonment "shall not be less than 6 months". s 96A(2): the same for
-- "(a) 2 or more offences under this section ...; or (b) one offence under this section and one offence under section 96".
-- Gloss: repeat evaders face at least six months if imprisoned. The ss 37M and 37S offences counted there are not encoded.
GIVEN `my convictions under s 96` IS A NUMBER
      `my convictions under s 96A` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must any imprisonment I am liable to be at least 6 months` IF
        `my convictions under s 96` AT LEAST 3
    OR  `my convictions under s 96A` AT LEAST 2
    OR  (`my convictions under s 96` AT LEAST 1 AND `my convictions under s 96A` AT LEAST 1)

-- s 96(3): "Whenever in any proceedings under this section it is proved that any false statement or entry is made in any return
-- ... by or on behalf of any person, that person is presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have made that false statement or
-- entry with intent to evade tax".
-- Gloss: once a false entry in my return is proved, it is for me to show I did not mean to evade.
GIVEN `a false statement in my return is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have proved I did not intend to evade tax` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I presumed to have intended to evade tax` IF
    `a false statement in my return is proved` AND NOT `I have proved I did not intend to evade tax`

-- s 99: "The institution of proceedings for, or the imposition of, a penalty, fine or term of imprisonment under this Act does not
-- relieve any person from liability to payment of any tax".
GIVEN `I have been penalised, fined or imprisoned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does a penalty free me from paying the tax` IF FALSE
